<title>SWITZERLAND: ALPINE SKIING-RIEGLER WINS SLALOM.</title>
<headline>ALPINE SKIING-RIEGLER WINS SLALOM.</headline>
<dateline>CRANS MONTANA, Switzerland 1996-12-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Claudia Riegler of New Zealand won the women's World Cup slalom race on Saturday in an unoffical two-run combined time of one minute, 29.83 seconds.</p>
<p>Pernilla Wiberg of Sweden was second and Patricia Chauvet of France third, also according to provisional results.</p>
